0:20Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19044) - Multi-window, 4 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7283) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen ***AN*** editor feature profile is active, ClassDB will print `ERROR: Cannot get class 'MyCustomResource'` one or multiple times every time a re-import happens for a file that's been imported into a `MyCustomResource` type by an EditorImportPlugin implementation.\n\nThe content of the editor feature profile is arbitrary; the error persists even though all Node, Class, and Feature Sets are enabled.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Download the MRP project archive.\n2. Open it with the Godot Editor 4.4.1.\n3. Check to ensure the `MRP.mrpdoc` is imported correctly.\n4. Import the included feature profile in the `Editor/Managed Editor Features`.\n5. Reimport the `MRP.mrpdoc` to observe the issue.\n\nContext: The `MRP.mrpdoc` itself is a UTF-8 encoded text file.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d4d6c48-56ba-4d03-9712-c6b92ee4f449\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[Mrp-cannot-get-custom-importer-class.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20278541/Mrp-cannot-get-custom-importer-class.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https:/